index 00000000..c4925867
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/FIXED_PLACEMENT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Opt-in fixed expert budget diagnostic
+
+DS4_EXPERT_BUDGET_BYTES accepts a positive decimal integer through9007199254740991.
+It requires CUDA, one GPU/group/member and --no-expert-cache. It preserves the
+existing safe-memory calculation and fails when the requested budget exceeds
+that bound; it never silently reduces the requested value. Unset preserves the
+existing path. The chosen bytes cover the entire expert budget, including any
+loaded draft experts. Freeze the same model, drafting load mode and expert-profile
+file as well as the byte value for comparisons.
+
+The startup emits requested/effective/safe bytes and per-layer plus aggregate
+FNV1a64 hashes of layer index, expert count, resident count and expert-to-slot
+mapping. The hash is diagnostic identity, not a cryptographic integrity proof.
+Compare every layer hash, effective chunk and resources across fresh processes.
+A fixed expert map does not establish deterministic kernels or model correctness.
+The budget does not freeze all scratch allocations or remove host memory guards.
+
+This is an unmeasured diagnostic candidate. It responds to observed fresh-process
+placement variation; that variation has not been proved to cause token mismatch.
